{
  "name": "fish",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-07, the sculpt overlay; generator scratchpad sc/sea2/gen/fish.py): a pond fish, 0.25-0.45 m -- a roach's fusiform body, deepest a third of the way back (its depth ~27% of its standard length), a small blunt head over a little terminal mouth, the gill cover's edge carved, a big eye; scales in staggered rows, each one's back edge rimmed dark (the coat pattern `rowscales`, coatpat.js 32: some 42 along the lateral line), the lateral line painted; the dorsal over the pelvics, the anal behind, low pectorals and a deeply FORKED tail with pointed lobes on the tail's bone (it beats) -- the fins thin plates, their corners rounded, faint rays fanning from each root (`finrays`, coatpat.js 33); countershaded (`shade`): the back the coat's dark, a pale silver belly. A SWIMMER: it rides the flier plumbing -- its `fly` alt its depth under the surface, its speed and tail-beat rate (index.html addSwimmer). Drawn at three sizes and in its coats by its seed (species.js makeFish).",
  "_params": "k: the fish's size -- every length of the rig is written over it, and the overlay (written at k = 1) is scaled by it through `sculptScale` (bodyspec.js scaleOverlay). The game draws three sizes, k = 0.8, 1.15 and 1.5, and one of the coats, both picked by the fish's seed (species.js makeFish).",
